{
  "video": {
    "id": "BwIZ0VzKEDg",
    "title": "First-order Constant Coefficient Linear ODE's | MIT 18.03SC Differential Equations, Fall 2011",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BwIZ0VzKEDg",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 798,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 263,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 8.79,
      "end": 8.8,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Hi everyone. Welcome back."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 8.8,
      "end": 10.31,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "So, today we're going to take a look at"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 10.32,
      "end": 11.75,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "first-order linear differential"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 11.76,
      "end": 14.35,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "equations with constant coefficients."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 14.36,
      "end": 15.51,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "And specifically, we're going to use"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 15.52,
      "end": 18.23,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "integrating factors to solve them."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 18.24,
      "end": 19.11,
      "duration": 0.87,
      "text": "So, the equation that we're going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 19.12,
      "end": 23.47,
      "duration": 4.35,
      "text": "solve today is x. + kx = 1."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 23.48,
      "end": 24.55,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "And then in part B, we're going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 24.56,
      "end": 26.43,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "change the right-hand side to e to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 26.44,
      "end": 29.19,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "minus 5t."
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 29.2,
      "end": 31.11,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "And then in part C, we're asked to use"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 31.12,
      "end": 34.19,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "the superposition principle to solve x."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 34.2,
      "end": 36.87,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "+ kx = 4"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 36.88,
      "end": 40.19,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "plus 7e to the minus 5t."
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 40.2,
      "end": 41.27,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "So, let you think about this for a"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 41.28,
      "end": 56.83,
      "duration": 15.55,
      "text": "moment and I'll come back in a second."
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 59.83,
      "end": 59.84,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Hi everyone. Welcome back."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 59.84,
      "end": 60.71,
      "duration": 0.87,
      "text": "So,"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 60.72,
      "end": 62.63,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "I should mention that uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 62.64,
      "end": 64.35,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "every first-order linear differential"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 64.36,
      "end": 65.75,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "equation, whether it has constant"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 65.76,
      "end": 67.43,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "coefficients or not, can always be"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 67.44,
      "end": 70.63,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "solved using an integrating factor."
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 70.64,
      "end": 71.83,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "However, in this case, we have a"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 71.84,
      "end": 73.03,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "constant coefficient, which is"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 73.04,
      "end": 75.11,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "particularly nice. And later on in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 75.12,
      "end": 76.55,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "course, we're going to learn some even"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 76.56,
      "end": 79.43,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "better ways or quicker ways to solve uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 79.44,
      "end": 80.71,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "linear differential equations with"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 80.72,
      "end": 82.35,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "constant coefficients."
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 82.36,
      "end": 83.59,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "But for today, we're asked to use an"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 83.6,
      "end": 88.35,
      "duration": 4.75,
      "text": "integrating factor."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 90.91,
      "end": 90.92,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So, for part A,"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 90.92,
      "end": 96.03,
      "duration": 5.11,
      "text": "we have the equation x. + kx"
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 97.35,
      "end": 97.36,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "equals 1."
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 97.36,
      "end": 98.63,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "And the first step is to compute the"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 98.64,
      "end": 101.99,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "integrating factor."
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 104.15,
      "end": 104.16,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So, the integrating factor,"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 104.16,
      "end": 107.99,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "which I'll call g(t),"
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 110.95,
      "end": 110.96,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "it's always going to be an exponential"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 110.96,
      "end": 113.07,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "of the integral"
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 113.08,
      "end": 114.75,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "of the function that appears in front of"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 114.76,
      "end": 117.71,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "x."
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 119.19,
      "end": 119.2,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So, in this case, the function is just a"
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 119.2,
      "end": 123.35,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "constant, it's K."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 125.19,
      "end": 125.2,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So we have K"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 125.2,
      "end": 128.91,
      "duration": 3.71,
      "text": "DT"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 136.99,
      "end": 137.0,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So once we have the integrating factor"
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 137.0,
      "end": 139.31,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "we just multiply our equation through by"
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 139.32,
      "end": 158.87,
      "duration": 19.55,
      "text": "G of T."
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 161.55,
      "end": 161.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And by construction"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 161.56,
      "end": 164.87,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "what the integrating factor does"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 164.88,
      "end": 166.47,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "is it lets us combine these two terms on"
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 166.48,
      "end": 167.949,
      "duration": 1.469,
      "text": "the left-hand side"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 167.959,
      "end": 173.83,
      "duration": 5.871,
      "text": "into an exact derivative."
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 175.99,
      "end": 176.0,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So these two terms are actually"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 176.0,
      "end": 179.63,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "the time derivative of"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 179.64,
      "end": 182.19,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "the product X"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 182.2,
      "end": 184.11,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "times the integrating factor"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 184.12,
      "end": 188.35,
      "duration": 4.23,
      "text": "E to the KT."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 189.47,
      "end": 189.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And then on the right-hand side we just"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 189.48,
      "end": 192.03,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "have E to the KT."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 192.04,
      "end": 193.27,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "So we can just go ahead and integrate"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 193.28,
      "end": 202.07,
      "duration": 8.79,
      "text": "both sides of the equation."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 203.67,
      "end": 203.68,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And when we do that"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 203.68,
      "end": 205.03,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "the right-hand side becomes the integral"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 205.04,
      "end": 208.55,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "of KT"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 211.229,
      "end": 211.239,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "which is 1 over K"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 211.239,
      "end": 213.79,
      "duration": 2.551,
      "text": "E to the KT"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 213.8,
      "end": 217.509,
      "duration": 3.709,
      "text": "plus a constant of integration."
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 219.59,
      "end": 219.6,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And now just isolate X, I can multiply"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 219.6,
      "end": 221.55,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "through by E to the KT, sorry, divide"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 221.56,
      "end": 229.83,
      "duration": 8.27,
      "text": "through by E to the KT."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 232.35,
      "end": 232.36,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And I obtain 1 over K"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 232.36,
      "end": 235.87,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "plus a constant"
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 248.63,
      "end": 248.64,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay, so this concludes part A."
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 248.64,
      "end": 252.07,
      "duration": 3.43,
      "text": "For part B,"
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 262.03,
      "end": 262.04,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "= e to the -5t."
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 262.04,
      "end": 263.75,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "So, if we take a look at this equation,"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 263.76,
      "end": 265.27,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "the only thing that we've changed is the"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 265.28,
      "end": 266.99,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "right-hand side. We haven't changed the"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 267.0,
      "end": 271.11,
      "duration": 4.11,
      "text": "left-hand side."
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 272.75,
      "end": 272.76,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And again, if we compute the integrating"
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 272.76,
      "end": 274.31,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "factor,"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 274.32,
      "end": 275.51,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "well, we note that it's the same"
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 275.52,
      "end": 280.43,
      "duration": 4.91,
      "text": "integrating factor as in part A."
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 282.15,
      "end": 282.16,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And the reason is that the integrating"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 282.16,
      "end": 283.63,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "factor only depends on the left-hand"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 283.64,
      "end": 285.15,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "side. It only depends on the linear"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 285.16,
      "end": 289.79,
      "duration": 4.63,
      "text": "terms."
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 291.15,
      "end": 291.16,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So, I can multiply the equation through"
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 291.16,
      "end": 300.11,
      "duration": 8.95,
      "text": "by the integrating factor again."
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 302.75,
      "end": 302.76,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And when I do this,"
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 302.76,
      "end": 303.909,
      "duration": 1.149,
      "text": "I'll just combine the terms on the"
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 303.919,
      "end": 307.27,
      "duration": 3.351,
      "text": "right-hand side."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 316.11,
      "end": 316.12,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And again, by construction, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 316.12,
      "end": 319.15,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "left-hand side"
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 336.11,
      "end": 336.12,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And now we can go ahead and integrate"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 336.12,
      "end": 351.63,
      "duration": 15.51,
      "text": "both sides."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 354.03,
      "end": 354.04,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay, so if we integrate this"
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 354.04,
      "end": 358.31,
      "duration": 4.27,
      "text": "we end up getting 1 over K minus 5"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 369.39,
      "end": 369.4,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And if we step back and take a look at"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 369.4,
      "end": 370.91,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "this for a second"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 370.92,
      "end": 372.79,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "we see that when K equals 5 we have a"
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 372.8,
      "end": 374.47,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "problem."
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 374.48,
      "end": 377.23,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "Particularly the denominator vanishes"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 377.24,
      "end": 380.55,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "which would give us 1 over 0."
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 380.56,
      "end": 382.43,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "So this equation"
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 382.44,
      "end": 384.03,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "this right hand side actually only holds"
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 384.04,
      "end": 387.03,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "when K is not equal to 5."
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 387.04,
      "end": 388.95,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "So this is only valid for K not equal to"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 388.96,
      "end": 393.95,
      "duration": 4.99,
      "text": "5."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 395.39,
      "end": 395.4,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So the question is what happens when K"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 395.4,
      "end": 405.15,
      "duration": 9.75,
      "text": "equals to 5?"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 406.99,
      "end": 407.0,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And in this case"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 407.0,
      "end": 409.11,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "we would have X"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 409.12,
      "end": 413.07,
      "duration": 3.95,
      "text": "e to the KT"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 415.47,
      "end": 415.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "times the integral of 1"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 415.48,
      "end": 418.23,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "dt"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 419.55,
      "end": 419.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "which would just give us T plus a"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 419.56,
      "end": 428.07,
      "duration": 8.51,
      "text": "constant C."
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 430.47,
      "end": 430.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So in this case we would have"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 430.48,
      "end": 435.03,
      "duration": 4.55,
      "text": "T e to the minus KT"
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 438.909,
      "end": 438.919,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "plus C e to the minus KT."
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 438.919,
      "end": 443.55,
      "duration": 4.631,
      "text": "And this is when K is equal to 5."
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 451.75,
      "end": 451.76,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "well we have the solution worked out"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 451.76,
      "end": 452.71,
      "duration": 0.95,
      "text": "already"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 452.72,
      "end": 455.63,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "so we can just isolate X"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 455.64,
      "end": 459.35,
      "duration": 3.71,
      "text": "and divide through by"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 468.23,
      "end": 468.24,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "and we have 1 over k minus 5"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 468.24,
      "end": 471.43,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "e to the minus 5 t"
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 471.44,
      "end": 472.79,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "plus c"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 472.8,
      "end": 481.55,
      "duration": 8.75,
      "text": "e to the minus k t."
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 482.55,
      "end": 482.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 482.56,
      "end": 485.27,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "And this concludes part B."
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 485.28,
      "end": 489.03,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "So, the solution for uh k equal to 5"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 489.04,
      "end": 492.15,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "is t e to the minus k t, which would be"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 492.16,
      "end": 493.99,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "e to the minus 5 t"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 494.0,
      "end": 495.63,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "plus the constant"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 495.64,
      "end": 499.23,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "c times e to the minus 5 t."
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 499.24,
      "end": 501.35,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "And when k is not equal to 5, we have 1"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 501.36,
      "end": 504.63,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "over k minus 5 e to the minus 5 t plus c"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 504.64,
      "end": 506.71,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "e to the minus k t."
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 506.72,
      "end": 507.79,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "So, I'd just like to point out a few"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 507.8,
      "end": 508.95,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "things"
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 508.96,
      "end": 510.55,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "uh between the solutions for part A and"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 510.56,
      "end": 512.149,
      "duration": 1.589,
      "text": "for part B."
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 512.159,
      "end": 513.469,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "First off,"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 513.479,
      "end": 516.75,
      "duration": 3.271,
      "text": "we note that both part A and part B"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 516.76,
      "end": 519.07,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "share a common solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 519.08,
      "end": 521.99,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "of the form constant c"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 522.0,
      "end": 524.029,
      "duration": 2.029,
      "text": "times e to the minus k t. So, this is a"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 524.039,
      "end": 526.07,
      "duration": 2.031,
      "text": "term that appears in the solution for"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 526.08,
      "end": 528.51,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "both part A and for part B."
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 528.52,
      "end": 530.39,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "The reason is this can be thought of as"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 530.4,
      "end": 532.15,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "the homogeneous solution to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 532.16,
      "end": 533.829,
      "duration": 1.669,
      "text": "differential equation."
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 533.839,
      "end": 535.19,
      "duration": 1.351,
      "text": "This is the term that solves the"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 535.2,
      "end": 536.39,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "differential equation when the"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 536.4,
      "end": 540.59,
      "duration": 4.19,
      "text": "right-hand side is set to zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 543.27,
      "end": 543.28,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Uh secondly, in part B, if we take a"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 543.28,
      "end": 544.31,
      "duration": 1.03,
      "text": "look"
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 544.32,
      "end": 546.71,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "when k is equal to when k is not equal"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 546.72,
      "end": 548.03,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "to 5,"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 548.04,
      "end": 550.23,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "we have the term, which is a constant,"
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 550.24,
      "end": 552.55,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "times e to the minus 5 t."
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 552.56,
      "end": 553.99,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "However,"
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 554.0,
      "end": 557.71,
      "duration": 3.71,
      "text": "when we have k equal to 5,"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 557.72,
      "end": 560.91,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "uh what happens is"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 560.92,
      "end": 561.91,
      "duration": 0.99,
      "text": "well,"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 561.92,
      "end": 563.43,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "what happens is"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 563.44,
      "end": 566.51,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "we have a term, which essentially occurs"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 566.52,
      "end": 568.19,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "from forcing the differential equation"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 568.2,
      "end": 569.829,
      "duration": 1.629,
      "text": "on resonance,"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 569.839,
      "end": 572.07,
      "duration": 2.231,
      "text": "which gives us an extra factor of t"
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 572.08,
      "end": 575.07,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "times e to the minus 5 t."
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 575.08,
      "end": 576.35,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "And we'll see more about resonance in"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 576.36,
      "end": 578.31,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "the future."
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 578.32,
      "end": 581.91,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "Okay, so for part C,"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 594.67,
      "end": 594.68,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "to solve the differential equation x."
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 594.68,
      "end": 596.99,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "+ kx"
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 597.0,
      "end": 598.83,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "= 4"
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 598.84,
      "end": 600.59,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "+ 7"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 600.6,
      "end": 604.27,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "e to the minus 5t."
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 605.15,
      "end": 605.16,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Now, if we take a look at this"
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 605.16,
      "end": 607.07,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "differential equation, we already know"
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 607.08,
      "end": 608.99,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "the solution when the right-hand side is"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 609.0,
      "end": 610.95,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "1 and when the right-hand side is e to"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 610.96,
      "end": 613.23,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "the minus 5t."
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 613.24,
      "end": 614.59,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "So, we've changed the right-hand side"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 614.6,
      "end": 618.83,
      "duration": 4.23,
      "text": "now, so it's 4 * 1 + 7 * e to the minus"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 618.84,
      "end": 620.39,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "5t."
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 620.4,
      "end": 621.91,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "So, what's the total solution going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 621.92,
      "end": 622.71,
      "duration": 0.79,
      "text": "be?"
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 622.72,
      "end": 625.99,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "Well, it's going to be 4 * our solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 626.0,
      "end": 628.15,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "when the right-hand side was 1"
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 628.16,
      "end": 631.03,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "+ 7 * the solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 631.04,
      "end": 632.43,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "when the right-hand side was e to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 632.44,
      "end": 633.87,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "minus 5t."
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 633.88,
      "end": 635.03,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "This is one of the beautiful things"
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 635.04,
      "end": 637.79,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "about linear equations. When we add two"
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 637.8,
      "end": 639.95,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "forcings to the right-hand side, our"
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 639.96,
      "end": 641.71,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "total solution is just going to be the"
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 641.72,
      "end": 643.51,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "sum of the solutions to the individual"
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 643.52,
      "end": 646.35,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "terms."
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 648.43,
      "end": 648.44,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 648.44,
      "end": 652.47,
      "duration": 4.03,
      "text": "So, what this means is our solution x"
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 652.48,
      "end": 656.11,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "is going to be 4 *"
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 656.12,
      "end": 657.43,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "the solution when the right-hand side"
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 657.44,
      "end": 658.91,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "was 1."
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 658.92,
      "end": 660.87,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "And in that case,"
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 660.88,
      "end": 662.829,
      "duration": 1.949,
      "text": "it was 1 over k"
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 662.839,
      "end": 665.07,
      "duration": 2.231,
      "text": "+ c"
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 665.08,
      "end": 669.71,
      "duration": 4.63,
      "text": "e to the minus kt."
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 675.63,
      "end": 675.64,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "7 * the solution when the right-hand"
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 675.64,
      "end": 678.71,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "side was e to the minus 5t."
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 678.72,
      "end": 680.95,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "And when k was not equal to 5,"
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 680.96,
      "end": 684.11,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "this becomes 1 over k minus 5"
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 684.12,
      "end": 686.79,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "e to the minus 5t"
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 686.8,
      "end": 692.43,
      "duration": 5.63,
      "text": "+ c e to the minus kt."
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 693.67,
      "end": 693.68,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So, if we take a look at the sum of"
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 693.68,
      "end": 696.67,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "these two terms,"
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 698.55,
      "end": 698.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "I'll denote the constants the two"
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 698.56,
      "end": 700.95,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "constants as C1 and C2. We actually have"
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 700.96,
      "end": 705.43,
      "duration": 4.47,
      "text": "4 * C1 + 7 * C2."
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 705.44,
      "end": 706.55,
      "duration": 1.11,
      "text": "That's just going to give us a new"
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 706.56,
      "end": 708.91,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "constant C3."
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 708.92,
      "end": 710.71,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "So in general,"
    },
    {
      "index": 229,
      "start": 710.72,
      "end": 713.11,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "this becomes 4"
    },
    {
      "index": 230,
      "start": 713.12,
      "end": 715.83,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "over K"
    },
    {
      "index": 231,
      "start": 719.27,
      "end": 719.28,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "+ 1 over K - 5"
    },
    {
      "index": 232,
      "start": 719.28,
      "end": 721.99,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "e to the - 5t"
    },
    {
      "index": 233,
      "start": 722.0,
      "end": 723.19,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "+"
    },
    {
      "index": 234,
      "start": 723.2,
      "end": 727.35,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "a constant C"
    },
    {
      "index": 235,
      "start": 732.87,
      "end": 732.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So I can just recombine"
    },
    {
      "index": 236,
      "start": 732.88,
      "end": 735.95,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "the 4 C e to the - Kt and the 7 C e to"
    },
    {
      "index": 237,
      "start": 735.96,
      "end": 737.59,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "the - Kt."
    },
    {
      "index": 238,
      "start": 737.6,
      "end": 738.83,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "That together just gives me a new"
    },
    {
      "index": 239,
      "start": 738.84,
      "end": 742.63,
      "duration": 3.79,
      "text": "constant C3 * e to the - Kt."
    },
    {
      "index": 240,
      "start": 742.64,
      "end": 744.79,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "And this is the solution when K is not"
    },
    {
      "index": 241,
      "start": 744.8,
      "end": 746.87,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "equal to 5."
    },
    {
      "index": 242,
      "start": 746.88,
      "end": 749.19,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "When K equals to 5, what we do is we"
    },
    {
      "index": 243,
      "start": 749.2,
      "end": 751.47,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "just replace this term"
    },
    {
      "index": 244,
      "start": 751.48,
      "end": 754.71,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "with t e to the - Kt."
    },
    {
      "index": 245,
      "start": 754.72,
      "end": 757.67,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "So this is when K is not"
    },
    {
      "index": 246,
      "start": 757.68,
      "end": 763.15,
      "duration": 5.47,
      "text": "equal to 5."
    },
    {
      "index": 247,
      "start": 770.67,
      "end": 770.68,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 248,
      "start": 770.68,
      "end": 772.23,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "So I'll just conclude there."
    },
    {
      "index": 249,
      "start": 772.24,
      "end": 774.47,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "And uh for summary, we've taken a look"
    },
    {
      "index": 250,
      "start": 774.48,
      "end": 776.59,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "at a couple of or a first-order linear"
    },
    {
      "index": 251,
      "start": 776.6,
      "end": 777.75,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "differential equation with a couple"
    },
    {
      "index": 252,
      "start": 777.76,
      "end": 779.55,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "different right-hand sides."
    },
    {
      "index": 253,
      "start": 779.56,
      "end": 780.99,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "We've solved them using an integrating"
    },
    {
      "index": 254,
      "start": 781.0,
      "end": 782.59,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "factor."
    },
    {
      "index": 255,
      "start": 782.6,
      "end": 783.829,
      "duration": 1.229,
      "text": "And then what we've done is we've used"
    },
    {
      "index": 256,
      "start": 783.839,
      "end": 785.87,
      "duration": 2.031,
      "text": "the superposition principle"
    },
    {
      "index": 257,
      "start": 785.88,
      "end": 788.03,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "to solve the same ODE for a right-hand"
    },
    {
      "index": 258,
      "start": 788.04,
      "end": 790.31,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "side which is the superposition"
    },
    {
      "index": 259,
      "start": 790.32,
      "end": 792.15,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "of multiples of the functions that we've"
    },
    {
      "index": 260,
      "start": 792.16,
      "end": 795.31,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "had in part A and for part B."
    },
    {
      "index": 261,
      "start": 795.32,
      "end": 796.87,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "So I'd like to conclude here and I'll"
    },
    {
      "index": 262,
      "start": 796.88,
      "end": 799.64,
      "duration": 2.76,
      "text": "see you next time."
    }
  ],
  "course": {
    "category": "Mathematics",
    "title": "Differential Equations",
    "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL64BDFBDA2AF24F7E"
  }
}